              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मँगाना — mãgānā — \"to send for; to order (to be brought)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हमने कमरे में चाय मँगाई। hamne kamre meṁ cāy mãgāī. We ordered tea to our room."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने खाना मँगाया, usne khānā mãgāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मँगाना (mãgānā) is the causative partner of माँगना, \"to ask for\", which goes back to Sanskrit mārgati, \"seeks, requests\" (CDIAL 10074): you ask for a thing to be brought to you."
            }
          ]
